@page "/amazon-order-scraper"

<PageTitle>Amazon Order Scraper</PageTitle>

<h1>Amazon Order Scraper Bookmarklet</h1>

<p>
    When an Amazon order confirmation email doesn't include item details (this happens often
    now), the <a href="review-queue">Review Queue</a> flags the item as needing review. This
    bookmarklet reads the exact item title, price, and quantity straight off the Amazon
    order-details page itself and copies it to your clipboard - paste it into the Review
    Queue and every item in the order gets filled in automatically, no typing required.
</p>

<p>
    A screenshot of the order page still works too, if you'd rather use that - this is just
    the faster, more exact option when it works.
</p>

<h2>1. Install the bookmarklet</h2>

<p>
    Drag this link to your browser's bookmarks bar (show it first with Ctrl+Shift+B if it's
    hidden), or right-click it and choose "Bookmark Link":
</p>

<p>
    <a id="bookmarklet-link" href="@BookmarkletUrl"
       style="display: inline-block; padding: 8px 16px; background: #0969da; color: white; border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;">
        📋 Scrape Amazon Order
    </a>
</p>

<h2>2. Use it</h2>

<ol>
    <li>Open the order's page on Amazon (the Review Queue's "View on Amazon" link for that item goes straight there).</li>
    <li>Click the <strong>Scrape Amazon Order</strong> bookmark you just installed.</li>
    <li>You'll see an alert confirming what it found, and it copies that to your clipboard.</li>
    <li>Switch back to the <a href="review-queue">Review Queue</a> tab, click <strong>Paste screenshot / order data</strong> on that item, and paste (Ctrl+V or Cmd+V).</li>
</ol>

<p>
    If the order has more than one item, every item is applied automatically - the first
    fills in the item that was flagged, and the rest are added the same way "+ Add another
    item" would.
</p>

<h2>If something looks wrong</h2>

<p>
    If the alert says "found 0 items," it copies way more items than the order actually has
    (Amazon's "Products related to your order" recommendation carousel has gotten scraped
    along with the real item a couple of times before - each occurrence got fixed, but a
    new one showing up again isn't out of the question), or the title/price/quantity doesn't
    look right - <strong>don't paste it into the Review Queue</strong>. Let me know what you
    saw (or save the order page and share it, same as before) and it can be adjusted.
</p>

